James sought help with converting an Adobe Illustrator file into a shapefile in QGIS, encountering issues with invalid geometries when trying to merge polygons. I guided him through using the **Check Validity** tool to identify problems and recommended several methods for fixing invalid geometries, including utilizing the **Geometry Checker** plugin, selecting invalid geometries to modify, and employing `Fix Geometries` from the Processing Toolbox. When James reported that he couldn't find the **Geometry Checker** in the menus, I suggested opening the Processing Toolbox to search for it instead. I reiterated steps for running the tool and provided alternative methods for manual corrections and geometry simplification. I encouraged James to follow the repair processes to prepare his data for successful merging and final export as a shapefile.
